        <h2 id="why-wheel">1. Why a Wheel Beats a Standard Party Game</h2>

        <p>
          Board games, card games, and charades all run on a fixed structure
          with a beginning and an end. A spin wheel runs differently — in short,
          self-contained bursts, each one with its own build-up and payoff,
          which is exactly the rhythm a party actually needs.
        </p>

        <ul class="uc-list">
          <li>
            <div class="uc-icon">🎯</div>
            <div class="uc-body">
              <strong>Nobody needs the rules explained</strong>
              <span
